 "title": "Documentation: CR-142, schema migration, BUG-77 findings, auth corrections",
 "description": "Read each file first and edit it in place, keeping the existing structure.\ndocs/API.md: replace 'Authentication: none' with the fact that X-API-Key (API_KEY setting, fail-closed, 401 {\"detail\": \"Invalid or missing API key\"}) is required for all /api/links* endpoints, while GET/HEAD /{code} and the probes are public. POST /api/links: document alias (3-32 [A-Za-z0-9_-], case-sensitive, stored as `code`, immutable) and expires_at (ISO-8601 date-time, naive = UTC, must be in the future, immutable, no maximum). Responses 201/400/401/409 ('Alias already in use' or idempotency payload mismatch)/422 (list detail for format errors; 'Alias is reserved'; 'expires_at must be in the future')/503. Response fields expires_at (UTC 'Z' or null) and is_expired. Reserved list (case-insensitive): api, docs, redoc, healthz, readyz, metrics, openapi.json, static, favicon.ico. The {code} format is widened to [A-Za-z0-9_-]{1,32} (other values give 404). Redirect 410: 'Link has been deactivated' (takes precedence) or 'Link has expired'; expired links still work for metadata/stats/delete; is_active stays true. request_hash = sha256(url) when alias and expires_at are absent, else sha256 of canonical JSON {alias, expires_at as UTC 'YYYY-MM-DDTHH:MM:SS.ffffffZ' or null, url} with sorted keys. Replays reflect current state.\ndocs/OPERATIONS.md: add links.expires_at (DATETIME NULL, naive UTC, NULL = never) to the data model. Startup: create_all followed by the automatic idempotent migration (one INFO log line on 'app.migrations' when the column is added; a concurrent duplicate-column error is tolerated; other errors fail startup). Manual SQL: `ALTER TABLE links ADD COLUMN expires_at DATETIME NULL` (SQLite/MySQL) and `ALTER TABLE links ADD COLUMN expires_at TIMESTAMP NULL` (PostgreSQL). Advise migrating once before a multi-instance rollout, and that rollback is safe (old code ignores the column). MySQL default collations make aliases case-insensitive (collisions and lookups). Correct the security notes (API key required, fail closed, constant-time compare).\nREADME.md: feature list gains custom aliases, link expiration and the reserved words; replace the 'no authentication' notice with the API-key requirement.\nCHANGELOG.md [Unreleased]: Added: CR-142 custom aliases (422 reserved/invalid, 409 taken), expires_at with 410 on expiry, expires_at/is_expired response fields, OpenAPI 409/410/422 and HEAD documented. Changed: schema change links.expires_at with automatic startup migration; {code} lookup accepts '-'/'_'; 'metrics' reserved; idempotency hash covers alias/expires_at (backwards compatible); alias insert race gives 409. Fixed: docs wrongly stated there was no authentication. BUG-77: investigated and not reproducible in validate_target_url (upper-case schemes are accepted unchanged; all javascript: variants are rejected); likely causes are a 401 from the missing API key, surrounding whitespace/newlines, or rows inserted directly into the DB; regression tests added; no behaviour change.",
